      "writtenOn": "2022-09-13T17:46:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The preferred way would be to create an alias node in the devicetree to define the sensor ID for the on-body detection.\n\n```\n/* From motionsense.dts */\naliases {\n    /* Use base accelerometer for on-body sensor */\n    on-body-sensor \u003d \u0026base_accel;\n};\n\naliases {\n    /* Use lid accelerometer for on-body sensor */\n    on-body-sensor \u003d \u0026lid_accel;\n};\n```\n\nThen you define the CONFIG_BODY_DETECTION_SENSOR macro:\n```\n#define CONFIG_BODY_DETECTION_SENSOR SENSOR_ID(DT_ALIAS(on_body_sensor))\n```\n\nAnd you can also delete `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_BODY_DETECTION_SENSOR` from the Kconfig definition.",
      "parentUuid": "112524d4_b0a96a7b",
